/**
 * Medical debt in collections on US credit reports (CFPB CCP + Urban Institute).
 *
 * Core question: How much collections debt on consumer credit files is medical,
 * and which states and credit-score bands carry the heaviest balances?
 *
 * Perimeter: CFPB Consumer Credit Panel medical-collections research
 * (Medical Debt Burden 2022; Paid & Low-Balance CCT July 2022; Recent Changes
 * Mar 2024; Market Snapshot Feb 2023) plus Urban Institute Debt in America /
 * August 2024 credit-bureau panel. Figures are credit-*report* medical
 * collections ??? not survey-reported medical bills, judgments, or unreported
 * provider balances. One-bureau CCP samples understate multi-bureau totals.
 *
 * Headline: Medical debt was ~58% of collections tradelines (Q2 2021) and still
 * ~$49B on files in Jun 2023; Urban puts ~4.1% of consumers (~9.7M) with a
 * medical collection in Aug 2024, with Oklahoma at 8.8%.
 */

export type Confidence = "disclosed" | "estimated" | "carried";

export const SOURCE_NOTE =
  "CFPB Consumer Credit Panel (1-in-48 sample from one nationwide CRA): Medical Debt Burden in the United States (Mar/Apr 2022, Appendix A Dec 2020 state shares and balances); Paid and Low-Balance Medical Collections CCT (Jul 2022); Market Snapshot on third-party collections (Feb 2023); Recent Changes in Medical Collections on Consumer Credit Records (Mar 2024, through Jun 2023). Urban Institute credit-bureau panel / Debt in America: Aug 2022???Aug 2024 prevalence path and Aug 2024 state rates (Oklahoma 8.8%, national 4.1%, ~9.7M consumers). Score-band prevalence rows are desk estimates calibrated to disclosed mean scores of medical-collection holders (CFPB Table 1; Urban Wire Aug 2022???2023 score path) ??? not a published CFPB score??state crosstab. Reporting-change removals erase items from credit files; they do not forgive the underlying bills.";

